{%- doc -%}
  Renders a product card that follows the GLOBAL card settings on a surface that has
  no block instance to read them from.

  The predictive-search popup is such a surface. sections/predictive-search.liquid is
  fetched only through the Section Rendering API and appears in no template JSON, so a
  static `_product-card` block there resolves zero configured child blocks and renders
  an empty, still-clickable shell. Native precedent for hand-rolling a card instead of
  delegating: sections/section-rendering-product-card.liquid, and the same reasoning is
  written out at length in sections/bmp-curated-product-card.liquid.

  Markup mirrors snippets/product-card.liquid plus the four card blocks it composes
  (_product-card-gallery, product-title, price, swatches) so this card inherits the
  same CSS. The `bmp-card-global-*` carrier classes are emitted UNCONDITIONALLY: there
  is no per-block bmp_use_global_style toggle on this surface, and following the global
  card is the whole point of the snippet.

  The gallery is delegated to snippets/card-gallery.liquid through its
  BMP-HOOK:card-param-surface params rather than reimplemented, so hover (all four
  bmp_card_hover_effect modes), the slideshow, product_card_carousel,
  show_second_image_on_hover, the global media ratio and the BMP product labels all
  come from one place and cannot drift from a collection-grid card.

  @param {object} product - The product to render
  @param {string} [image_sizes] - sizes attribute for the gallery media
  @param {string} [loading] - loading attribute for the featured media, e.g. 'lazy'
  @param {string} [product_view_context] - context recorded in the view event payload
  @param {string} [id_prefix] - namespace for the DOM ids this card mints

  @example
  {% render 'bmp-global-product-card', product: product, loading: 'lazy', id_prefix: 'ps-results-' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bmp_id_prefix = id_prefix | default: 'bmp-global-card-'

  # Title truncation: the global half of the mirror computed in
  # blocks/product-title.liquid. The class lands on the .text-block itself because
  # the clamp rule in assets/bmp-styles.css is `.bmp-title-clamp > *`.
  assign bmp_truncate_class = ''
  assign bmp_truncate_setting = settings.bmp_card_title_truncate_lines
  unless bmp_truncate_setting == blank or bmp_truncate_setting == 'none'
    assign bmp_truncate_class = 'bmp-title-clamp bmp-title-clamp--' | append: bmp_truncate_setting
  endunless


  assign bmp_selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  if settings.transition_to_main_product
    assign bmp_featured_image = bmp_selected_variant.featured_image
    if bmp_featured_image == blank
      assign bmp_featured_image = product.featured_media.preview_image
    endif
    if bmp_featured_image != blank
      assign bmp_featured_media_url = bmp_featured_image | image_url: width: 500
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank and product.id != blank -%}
  <div class="bmp-card-global-card">
    <product-card
      class="product-card"
      data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
      id="product-card-{{ bmp_id_prefix }}{{ product.id }}"
      {% if settings.transition_to_main_product %}
        data-product-transition="true"
        data-featured-media-url="{{ bmp_featured_media_url }}"
        on:click="/handleViewTransition"
      {% endif %}
      {% # theme-check-disable-next-line UnknownFilter %}
      view-event-payload="{{ product | standard_event_data: 'view', context: product_view_context | escape }}"
    >
      {%- comment -%}
        Both the `id` and the ref are load-bearing, and this anchor must stay the FIRST
        one in the card:
          - assets/product-card.js declares requiredRefs = ['productCardLink'] and
            throws from connectedCallback without it;
          - navigateToProduct reads link.getAttribute('id') and early-returns when it is
            absent, which is what makes clicks on the price row and the space beside the
            title navigate at all;
          - assets/predictive-search.js activates a keyboard-selected result with
            querySelector('a').click(), so the first anchor has to be the product link.
        The id is namespaced per list so the recently-viewed and results lists cannot
        mint the same id for the same product.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a
        id="{{ bmp_id_prefix | append: product.id | md5 }}"
        class="product-card__link"
        ref="productCardLink"
        href="{{ product.url }}"
        aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}"
      ></a>
      {%- comment -%}
        No quick add on this surface, and no --quick-add-* custom properties, because
        there is no quick-add element here to drive.

        This is the second documented exception. snippets/search-modal.liquid wraps the
        whole results area in <form class="predictive-search-form">, and
        snippets/quick-add.liquid opens its own {% form 'product' %} whenever it renders
        the Add button -- which it does for a single-variant product, or a
        single-option-with-swatches one. Nested forms are dropped by the HTML parser, so
        those hidden id / quantity inputs reparent onto the SEARCH form: the header's
        always-inline empty state would carry them on every page, and enabling
        settings.quick_add would turn the Add button into a submit of the search form,
        navigating to /search instead of adding to cart.

        The native Sale / Sold-out pill is absent for a different reason: the BMP label
        system owns every card overlay, and card-gallery renders it for us.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="product-card__content layout-panel-flex layout-panel-flex--column product-grid__card spacing-style border-style gap-style">
        {%- comment -%}
          bmp_lean_slides drops the hidden variant slides, which nothing on this surface
          can reveal -- there are no swatches here and card-hover-native-off disables the
          preview handlers. card-gallery decides whether that is safe: it ignores the
          request at second_image / next_variant, where those slides are the hover
          targets. Worth ~15 KB per page, since the empty state renders in the header on
          every one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'card-gallery',
          bmp_product: product,
          bmp_image_sizes: image_sizes,
          bmp_loading: loading,
          bmp_lean_slides: true
        -%}

        <div class="bmp-card-global-title">
          <a
            class="contents user-select-text"
            ref="productTitleLink"
            href="{{ product.url }}"
          >
            <div class="{{ bmp_truncate_class }} spacing-style text-block rte">
              <p role="heading" aria-level="3">{{ product.title }}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>

        <product-price
          class="text-block text-block--align-left text-left h6 spacing-style bmp-card-global-price"
          data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        >
          {%- render 'price',
            show_unit_price: true,
            product_resource: product,
            show_sale_price_first: settings.bmp_card_price_sale_first
          -%}

          {%- if settings.bmp_card_price_tax_info -%}
            <div class="tax-note">
              {%- if cart.duties_included and cart.taxes_included -%}
                {{ 'content.duties_and_taxes_included' | t }}
              {%- elsif cart.taxes_included -%}
                {{ 'content.taxes_included' | t }}
              {%- elsif cart.duties_included -%}
                {{ 'content.duties_included' | t }}
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if shop.shipping_policy.body != blank -%}
                {{ 'content.shipping_policy' | t }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if bmp_selected_variant != blank and settings.bmp_card_price_installments -%}
            <div class="installments">
              {%- assign bmp_installment_form_id = 'product-form-installment-' | append: bmp_id_prefix | append: product.id -%}
              {%- form 'product', product, id: bmp_installment_form_id, class: 'payment-terms' -%}
                <input
                  type="hidden"
                  name="id"
                  value="{{ bmp_selected_variant.id }}"
                >
                {{ form | payment_terms }}
              {%- endform -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </product-price>

        {%- comment -%}
          No swatch row, deliberately, and this is the one place this card does not
          follow a card block. Swatch PRESENCE is not a theme setting: it is a block
          instance in a template's JSON, and no template in this theme carries an
          enabled one — templates/collection.json has the swatches block disabled and
          every other template omits it. This surface has no template JSON to read, so
          there is nothing global to follow, and rendering swatches anyway would make
          the popup the only card in the theme that shows them. The BMP swatch STYLING
          settings (bmp_card_swatches_align / _pad_*) only shape a row that exists, so
          they are unaffected. If card swatches are ever enabled on the grid, add the
          product-swatches element here with the bmp-card-global-swatches class and the
          same option_any resolvable-value test blocks/swatches.liquid uses.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>
    </product-card>
  </div>

  {%- render 'product-card-styles' -%}
  {%- render 'payment-terms-styles' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    4.1.4 moved the .text-block base rules and the price family (.price,
    .tax-note, .installments, .unit-price) out of always-loaded base.css into
    render-scoped stylesheet snippets. This card emits .text-block classes
    DIRECTLY (title clamp wrapper, price line) rather than through
    snippets/text.liquid, and its typed-search render arrives through the
    Section Rendering API, which installs no response stylesheets — so both
    families must be preloaded here, exactly like the two renders above and
    like stock quick-add.liquid does for the same reason. The empty state
    renders this card inline in the header on every page, which is what puts
    these styles in scope before any typed result arrives.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'text-block-styles' -%}
  {%- render 'price-styles' -%}
{%- endif -%}
